    {
      "id": "MJUe",
      "code_hash": "7eff9c8b615d1bb6d93af4db74ce1b70",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"n-qubit-state-optimisation-sre-trajectory-generator\">\ud83e\uddea N-Qubit State Optimisation &amp; SRE Trajectory Generator</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This notebook generates <em>stabilizer R\u00e9nyi entropy</em> (SRE) trajectories for\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(N||)</marimo-tex>-qubit quantum states.  Starting from random <strong>stabilizer-gap</strong> initial\nstates it minimises the total <strong>Hilbert-Schmidt violation</strong> of the\nHildebrand separability criterion using JAX L-BFGS, while recording the\nexact SRE at every checkpoint via a Fast Walsh-Hadamard Transform (FWHT) kernel.</span>\n<blockquote>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Current Runtime Execution Mode:</strong> \ud83d\ude80 GPU-accelerated (CuPy + JAX CUDA)</span>\n</blockquote>\n<h3 id=\"workflow-at-a-glance\">Workflow at a glance</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Generate</strong> random almost-stabilizer initial states (symplectic circuit + Haar projection).</li>\n<li><strong>Optimise</strong> each state batch with vmapped L-BFGS.</li>\n<li><strong>Measure</strong> SRE at every <code>chunk_size</code> optimisation steps.</li>\n<li><strong>Save</strong> full trajectories (purity, violation, SRE, final states) to disk.</li>\n</ol></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
